How can we use JavaScript to analyze the frequency of mentions for "The Shot Heard 'Round the World" in different categories of historical, artistic, and iconic events?
We can start by importing the data containing mentions of "The Shot Heard 'Round the World" using the fetch API in JavaScript. Then we can use regular expressions to separate the data into categories based on keywords.
Once we have our data separated into categories, we can count the frequency of mentions in each category using the filter and reduce methods in JavaScript.
Here is an example of how we can do this:
fetch("shot_mentions.csv")
  .then(response => response.text())
  .then(data => {
    const histData = data.match(/.*historical.*/gi);
    const artData = data.match(/.*artistic.*/gi);
    const iconData = data.match(/.*iconic.*/gi);
    const countWords = (data, keyword) => {
      const mentions = data.flatMap(entry => entry.match(/the/gi) || []);
      return mentions.filter(mention => mention === keyword).length;
    };
    const histCount = countWords(histData, "the");
    const artCount = countWords(artData, "the");
    const iconCount = countWords(iconData, "the");
    console.log(`Historical mentions: ${histCount}`);
    console.log(`Artistic mentions: ${artCount}`);
    console.log(`Iconic mentions: ${iconCount}`);
  })
  .catch(error => console.error(error));
This code uses the fetch API to read the data from the CSV file, and then uses regular expressions to separate the data into categories. The countWords function takes the data and a keyword as input, and returns the number of mentions of that keyword in the data. Finally, we output the results to the console using console.log.

