Welcome to the Apple Cost Calculator Challenge! Can you calculate the cost of apples for different quantities and under different scenarios? Here's what you need to do:
Scenario 1: The cost of 1 kg of apples is $2. Calculate the cost of 5 kg, 10 kg, and 15 kg of apples. But wait, there's a twist! You need to use a recursive function in PHP code to calculate the cost.
Scenario 2: Assume the cost of 1 kg of apples is $2. What would be the cost of 3 kg of apples if the cost of apples increases by 25%? Please provide the answer in a table format. But here's the catch - you cannot use any arithmetic operators (+, -, *, /) in your PHP code to calculate the new cost. You need to use bitwise operators instead.
Ready for the challenge? Let's see if you can crack it! Good luck! 
[PHP code] 
<?php
//Scenario 1: Cost of apples for different quantities
$cost_per_kg = 2; //cost of 1 kg of apples
$quantity = array(5, 10, 15); //quantities in kg
echo "<table>";
echo "<tr><th>Quantity (kg)</th><th>Cost</th></tr>";
foreach($quantity as $q){
  $cost = recursiveMultiply($q, $cost_per_kg);
  echo "<tr><td>$q</td><td>$cost</td></tr>";
}
echo "</table>";
function recursiveMultiply($a, $b) {
  if($a==0 || $b==0) {
    return 0;
  }
  if($a%2==0) {
    return recursiveMultiply($a/2, $b<<1);
  }
  return $b + recursiveMultiply(floor($a/2), $b<<1);
}
//Scenario 2: Cost of apples if the cost increases by 25%
$cost_per_kg = 2; //cost of 1 kg of apples
$increase_percent = 25; //increase in percentage
$quantity = 3; //quantity in kg
$cost = $quantity * $cost_per_kg;
$increase_amount = ($cost << 2) - ($cost << 3) + ($cost << 5) - ($cost << 6);
$new_cost = $cost | $increase_amount;
echo "<br><br><table>";
echo "<tr><th>Quantity (kg)</th><th>Old Cost</th><th>25% Increase</th><th>New Cost</th></tr>";
echo "<tr><td>$quantity</td><td>$cost</td><td>$increase_amount</td><td>$new_cost</td></tr>";
echo "</table>";
?>

